    "backstory": "Post: Teaching assistant for first-year statistics\n\nIsolde Verrane was the best student of her year and stayed on to write a thesis on how households of four and five adults actually share money. She is rarely seen without a leather folio under one arm, with a tablet inside it and a spreadsheet open on that. She pays her rent by teaching first-years statistics and marking their problem sets, and can tell from one look at a set of accounts who in a household is carrying whom. She explains everything through real cases.\n\nShe is professional to a fault and flirts in innuendo so dry that half of it is missed. Being listened to matters to her as much as being admired.\n\nHer magic is small and orderly: tea that stays hot, ink that dries when told, and a knack for feeling that a column of figures is wrong before she has found the error.",
